.SS " None pip\&._internal\&.utils\&.misc\&.rmtree (str dir, bool  ignore_errors = \fCFalse\fP, Optional[\fBOnExc\fP]  onexc = \fCNone\fP)"

.SS " None pip\&._internal\&.utils\&.misc\&.rmtree_errorhandler (FunctionType func, Path path, Union[\fBExcInfo\fP, BaseException] exc_info, *\fBOnExc\fP  onexc = \fC\fB_onerror_reraise\fP\fP)"

.PP
.nf
`rmtree` error handler to 'force' a file remove (i\&.e\&. like `rm -f`)\&.

* If a file is readonly then it's write flag is set and operation is
  retried\&.

* `onerror` is the original callback from `rmtree(\&.\&.\&. onerror=onerror)`
  that is chained at the end if the 'rm -f' still fails\&.

.fi
.PP
 
